{%- comment -%}
  Jointwell v5 chrome, top half: the skip link, the dispatch bar and the
  header. Shared, so the advice pages, the policies and the app-proxy
  tracking page wear the same header as the landing page rather than
  falling through to Dawn's.

  Styled by assets/jw-v5.css, which layout/theme.liquid loads on every page
  that renders this.

  Parameters, all optional:
    phone  a support number. Left unset the header falls back to the email
           address rather than printing a placeholder that rings a stranger.
    email  defaults to the support address.
    home   '' on the homepage, so the nav links stay in-page; the root URL
           everywhere else, so they come back here first.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign jwh_phone = phone | default: settings.jw_support_phone
  assign jwh_email = email | default: settings.jw_support_email | default: 'support@velagoods.co.uk'
  assign jwh_home = home
  if template.name != 'index'
    assign jwh_home = routes.root_url
  endif

  comment
    The bar carries the sale, not the courier. Both figures come off the
    wrap's own variant, so the day the compare-at price is cleared in admin
    the bar falls back to the delivery line on its own rather than going on
    advertising a discount that has ended.
  endcomment
  assign jwh_handles = 'jointwell-heated-joint-massager,jointwell-heated-joint-wrap' | split: ','
  for h in jwh_handles
    assign c = all_products[h]
    if c != blank and c.id
      assign jwh_v = c.variants.first
      break
    endif
  endfor
  assign jwh_now = jwh_v.price
  assign jwh_was = jwh_v.compare_at_price
  if jwh_was == blank or jwh_was <= jwh_now
    assign jwh_was = jwh_now
  endif
  assign jwh_save = jwh_was | minus: jwh_now
-%}

<a class="skip-link" href="{{ jwh_home }}#main">Skip to the page</a>

{%- comment -%}
  ONE message. The delivery and returns promises live in the CTA bullets,
  and the dispatch date lives in the shipping question in the FAQ, which is
  where people go looking for it.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="batchbar">
  {%- if jwh_save > 0 -%}
    Sale: <b>{{ jwh_save | money_without_trailing_zeros }} off</b> the Jointwell wrap. {{ jwh_now | money_without_trailing_zeros }} instead of {{ jwh_was | money_without_trailing_zeros }}.
  {%- else -%}
    Free tracked UK delivery, and 90 days to send it back at our expense.
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

<header class="site">
  <div class="head-in">
    <a class="head-logo" href="{{ jwh_home | default: '#top' }}" aria-label="{{ shop.name }} home">
      <img src="{{ 'jointwell-logo.svg' | asset_url }}" alt="Jointwell" width="120" height="26">
    </a>
    <nav class="main">
      <a href="{{ jwh_home }}#how">How it works</a>
      <a href="{{ jwh_home }}#story">Paula's story</a>
      <a href="{{ jwh_home }}#reviews">Reviews</a>
      <a href="{{ jwh_home }}#faq">Questions</a>
    </nav>
    {%- comment -%}
      Was an 07 mobile. A landline reads as a company to this audience, and
      no number at all reads better than one that does not answer.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if jwh_phone != blank -%}
      <a class="head-tel" href="tel:{{ jwh_phone | remove: ' ' | remove: '-' }}">{{ jwh_phone }}<small>UK support, 9am to 5pm</small></a>
    {%- else -%}
      <a class="head-tel" href="mailto:{{ jwh_email }}">{{ jwh_email }}<small>UK support, 9am to 5pm</small></a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</header>
